{"content":"I have enough to answer confidently now.\n\nh06.\n\n**RPC handlers that transitively trigger an outbound HTTP call to a user-configured URL** (the URL comes from the recipient's stored `Webhook.Url`, i.e. a user-configured endpoint, `store.WebhooksUserSetting_Webhook`):\n\n- `APIV1Service.CreateMemo` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70`) → calls `DispatchMemoCreatedWebhook` (`memo_service.go:157`)\n- `APIV1Service.DeleteMemo` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:518`) → calls `DispatchMemoDeletedWebhook` (`memo_service.go:562`)\n- `APIV1Service.UpdateMemo` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:401`) → calls `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` (`memo_service.go:513`) → `DispatchMemoUpdatedWebhook` (`memo_update_helpers.go:67`)\n- `APIV1Service.SetMemoAttachments` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go:16`) → calls `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` (`memo_attachment_service.go:48`)\n- `APIV1Service.SetMemoRelations` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_relation_service.go:16`) → calls `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` (`memo_relation_service.go:48`)\n- `APIV1Service.CreateMemoComment` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:20`) → calls `DispatchMemoCommentCreatedWebhook` (`memo_service_comments.go:119`)\n\nAll of these `Dispatch*Webhook` helper methods (defined in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go`) fetch the user's stored webhooks via `s.Store.GetUserWebhooks`, build a `webhook.WebhookRequestPayload{URL: hook.Url, ...}`, and hand it to `webhook.PostAsync`.\n\n**Convergence function:** `Post` — `internal/webhook/webhook.go:120`\n\n`PostAsync` (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:184`) only enqueues onto `asyncPostQueue`; the four worker goroutines started in `init()` (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:42-55`) all pull from that queue and call `Post(payload)` (`webhook.go:46`), which is the single place that builds the `http.NewRequest` and issues it via `safeClient.Do(req)` (`webhook.go:126-152`) — i.e. every one of these RPC paths ultimately funnels through `Post`.","iteration":12,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
